From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bartosz Nitka <niteria@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 18:57:33 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: apple: t8132: describe the display power-down
 resources

Describe what a power-down of the internal display domains needs on
T8132:

- the PMGR register block up to the display CPU's power-gate retention
  registers at 0x2504c and 0x25070;
- the PS_PROT bank of clock protection slices, as a syscon;
- the internal display pipe's PMC interface enables (BWR and boost bit
  0), as a consumer-switched interface, since its power states are
  firmware-owned rather than a power domain.

No consumer uses them yet.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Bartosz Nitka <niteria@gmail.com>
(cherry picked from commit d49cf956704d3a58d65ad9d4aa362182f824ff90)
[j604: resolved by hand: a15y pmc node has no external interface children, so only pmc_disp0 is added (before clpc); ps_prot placed before aic in a15y node order; pmgr reg extension applied unchanged]
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-memory.dtsi | 12 ++++++++++++
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132.dtsi        |  9 ++++++++-
 2 files changed, 20 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-memory.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-memory.dtsi
index fea5b3a97d..4dd602f34b 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-memory.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-memory.dtsi
@@ -19,6 +19,18 @@
 		apple,pmp = <&pmp>;
 		status = "disabled";
 
+		/*
+		 * The internal display pipe's enables. Its power states are
+		 * firmware-owned, so they are not a power domain: its DCP
+		 * clears them before powering the pipe down and restores them.
+		 */
+		pmc_disp0: interface-disp0 {
+			label = "disp0-interface";
+			apple,consumer-switched;
+			apple,bwr-bit = <0>;
+			apple,boost-bit = <0>;
+		};
+
 		clpc: performance-controller@3 {
 			compatible = "apple,t8132-clpc";
 			reg = <3>;
diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132.dtsi
index 87f8ebbea1..22983d4ae9 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132.dtsi
@@ -409,7 +409,8 @@
 			compatible = "apple,t8132-pmgr", "apple,t8103-pmgr", "syscon", "simple-mfd";
 			#address-cells = <1>;
 			#size-cells = <1>;
-			reg = <0x3 0x80700000 0 0x14000>;
+			/* Up to the display CPU's power-gate retention registers. */
+			reg = <0x3 0x80700000 0 0x26000>;
 			/* child nodes are added in t8132-pmgr.dtsi */
 		};
 
@@ -458,6 +459,12 @@
 			power-domains = <&ps_pmp>, <&ps_pms_sram>;
 		};
 
+		/* Clock protection slices guarding power states of DART domains. */
+		ps_prot: syscon@38079c000 {
+			compatible = "apple,t8132-ps-prot", "syscon";
+			reg = <0x3 0x8079c000 0 0x4000>;
+		};
+
 		aic: interrupt-controller@381000000 {
 			compatible = "apple,t8132-aic3", "apple,t8122-aic3";
 			#interrupt-cells = <3>;
